# onnxruntime-node (pulled in by @huggingface/transformers) downloads its CUDA
# execution-provider binaries from GitHub in a postinstall on Linux x64. This
# service runs ONNX on the CPU, so skip that download: the v1.21.0 GPU tarball
# returns 404, which failed every `npm ci` here (CI and the Docker build).
# npm hands this to the install script as npm_config_onnxruntime_node_install_cuda.
# The Dockerfile copies this file in before `npm ci`.
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
